                <pb facs="0107" n="97" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv10/pg97"/>

                <head>Appendix 43</head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">Report of Finance Section Regarding
                        the Italian Situation</hi></p>
                <p>With reference to the memoranda laid by the Italian Representatives before the
                    Supreme Economic Council on the 25th February,<anchor n="5" xml:id="d9-f1"/> it
                    was agreed that the difficulties set forth in these memoranda would appear to be
                    not primarily financial. The commodities principally referred to are cereals,
                    meat, pork products, and coal. As regards cereals, the available finance exceeds
                    shipments up to date. This is also the case as regards pork. The Finance Section
                    is not aware of any financial difficulties as regards coal. There remains South
                    American meat. For the finance of this, a loan is in course of arrangement from
                    the Argentine Government. Pending completion of this loan, further shipments are
                    impossible.</p>
                <p>The Italian Representative pointed out that if this credit is not made available
                    immediately, there seems to be no way for Italy to get the meat, except through
                    some financial arrangements by the Associated Governments. He expressed his
                    anxiety that the matter should be treated as one of the utmost urgency.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
